# profiles/base.env — what the base has been changed to, and when.
#
# Written by bin/arm.sh promote. lib/config.sh applies this as the FLOOR:
# the environment, a profile and an arm all still outrank it. Delete a line
# to go back to the shipped default (profiles/default.env lists them all).
#
# promoted 2026-08-13: arm nofiller — cleanup cuts the author's sentence-opening
# hedges ("I think" above all).
#
# It stays HERE, in the directive slot, and was deliberately not folded into
# prompts/cleanup.md, because folding it in measurably weakened it. Same words,
# three positions, sentence-initial hedges left on the same seven recordings
# (30 uncut as the baseline): 5 from the directive slot, 12 from a bullet in the
# prompt's DO list, 8 from a dedicated section late in the prompt. The slot's
# power is its POSITION — instructions + anchor + DIRECTIVE + input puts it
# immediately before the transcript, where a mid-prompt rule competes with forty
# other rules. Churn stayed flat only in the slot version too.
#
# The cost of that choice: this occupies the cleanup directive slot, so a future
# cleanup experiment that sets CLEANUP_DIRECTIVE will REPLACE this file and
# silently revert the filler removal. Any such experiment must include this
# mandate in its own directive. That trap is the price of the better result.

CLEANUP_DIRECTIVE=$BLOG_REPO_DIR/profiles/directives/cleanup-nofiller.md
CURATE_DIRECTIVE=$BLOG_REPO_DIR/profiles/directives/tournament.md
GATE_TRACE=1
GLUE_MAX_WORDS=20
MAX_LONG=4
MAX_NEW=60
MAX_SHORT=8
NEW_SLACK_EVERY=6
VERBATIM_MIN=55
